and they need you to do the sorting yourself.

17:31.740 --> 17:34.060
This is the most elegant part of the system.

17:34.520 --> 17:36.280
They don't brand you by force anymore.

17:36.860 --> 17:39.600
They give you the iron and let you brand yourself.

17:40.180 --> 17:42.680
Pick a side, pick a label, pick an identity,

17:43.120 --> 17:45.720
put it in your bio, put it in your profile,

17:46.300 --> 17:47.360
defend it in the comments.

17:48.000 --> 17:50.340
That's you doing it all by yourself.

17:50.940 --> 17:53.180
Cialdini calls this commitment and consistency.

17:53.940 --> 17:56.520
Once you take a public position, even a small one,

17:57.160 --> 17:59.140
you experience crushing internal pressure

17:59.140 --> 18:01.520
to behave consistently with that position.

18:02.080 --> 18:03.220
Not because it's logical,

18:03.640 --> 18:06.080
because your identity is now attached to it.

18:06.580 --> 18:08.860
And this is how radicalization actually works.

18:09.380 --> 18:11.200
Not through a single moment of conversion,

18:11.960 --> 18:14.140
through a ratchet of small commitments.

18:15.140 --> 18:16.240
You know, picture this scenario.

18:16.240 --> 18:19.080
You share a mildly provocative mean.

18:19.640 --> 18:20.680
It's a little bit controversial.

18:20.920 --> 18:21.820
It's a small commitment.

18:22.260 --> 18:24.940
Then you join a group that shares similar content.

18:25.540 --> 18:26.800
That's the public commitment.

18:27.540 --> 18:30.180
Then you defend the group's position in an argument.

18:30.540 --> 18:32.240
That's identity commitment.

18:33.820 --> 18:35.180
Each step feels natural.

18:35.780 --> 18:38.220
Each step feels like your choice.

18:38.860 --> 18:41.540
By the time the content actually becomes extreme,

18:42.280 --> 18:44.520
you have too much identity invested in it

18:44.520 --> 18:45.760
to reverse your course.

18:46.700 --> 18:48.540
Because reversing course means admitting

18:48.540 --> 18:50.780
every step before was just wrong.

18:51.540 --> 18:53.640
The Chinese figured this out during the Korean War.

18:54.120 --> 18:56.280
They never beat American POWs.

18:56.420 --> 18:57.380
They didn't need to.

18:57.900 --> 18:59.680
They asked for tiny concessions.

19:00.280 --> 19:03.020
Write down one thing that isn't perfect about America.

19:03.920 --> 19:06.100
No reasonable person would refuse this.

19:06.540 --> 19:07.960
Then make a list.

19:08.740 --> 19:12.320
Then sign it and read it to your fellow prisoners.

19:13.100 --> 19:14.460
Each step was small,

19:15.040 --> 19:17.360
but the cumulative effect was devastating.

19:18.500 --> 19:20.760
American intelligence concluded that virtually

19:20.760 --> 19:24.940
all Chinese held POWs collaborated in some way.

19:25.280 --> 19:26.760
No physical coercion required.

19:27.220 --> 19:29.240
Just that small ratcheting system.

19:30.760 --> 19:33.160
I know what identity destruction looks like.

19:33.400 --> 19:35.280
My people lived through the original version.

19:36.100 --> 19:39.940
In 1879, Captain Richard Henry founded

19:39.940 --> 19:42.220
the Carlisle Indian Industrial School.

19:42.880 --> 19:46.360
13 years later, a national conference in 1892,

19:46.780 --> 19:49.780
he said five words that should make your blood freeze.

19:50.360 --> 19:52.580
Kill the Indian, save the man.

19:55.340 --> 19:59.280
For 150 years, 1819 to 1969,

19:59.900 --> 20:02.020
tens of thousands of indigenous children

20:02.020 --> 20:05.040
were taken from their families, often by force,

20:05.680 --> 20:07.540
sent to more than 400 boarding schools.

20:08.060 --> 20:11.360
What happened there was a systematic identity destruction.

20:12.520 --> 20:13.540
Our names were erased.

20:14.520 --> 20:17.240
A Yankton Dakota girl, said Carla Shaw,

20:17.800 --> 20:22.180
Redbird, was renamed Gertrude by missionaries.

20:22.540 --> 20:24.440
Children were forbidden to use their own names.

20:25.040 --> 20:28.580
Our hair was cut, and in our culture, hair is spiritual.

20:29.280 --> 20:30.120
That was deliberate.

20:30.880 --> 20:33.100
Our languages were beaten out of us.

20:33.740 --> 20:37.340
Children were physically, sexually, and spiritually abused

20:37.880 --> 20:39.500
for speaking their own tongue.

20:40.300 --> 20:42.660
Our spiritual practices were replaced with Christianity.

20:44.300 --> 20:46.360
We weren't being educated, as they say.

20:46.540 --> 20:49.940
We were being reformatted, like a fucking hard drive.

20:50.400 --> 20:52.680
Wiped and replaced with a fresh identity.

20:53.240 --> 20:55.120
Kill the Indian, save the man.

20:56.700 --> 20:58.220
And here's what haunts me.

20:58.600 --> 20:59.500
A survivor's testimony

20:59.500 --> 21:01.460
described what happened after the schools.

21:02.160 --> 21:05.780
Our grandmother recalled hearing the Oneida language

21:05.780 --> 21:07.080
spoken by the adults,

21:07.540 --> 21:09.860
but they chose not to teach it to their children

21:10.260 --> 21:11.980
because it was a source of trauma,

21:12.640 --> 21:15.020
because they had been told it was backwards,

21:15.900 --> 21:18.280
uncivilized, of the past,

21:19.760 --> 21:22.580
and that there was no utility in speaking it anymore.

21:24.780 --> 21:26.740
That brand was so deep,

21:27.380 --> 21:29.900
the brand started branding their own children.

21:30.600 --> 21:33.380
That's how you know the system works.

21:35.560 --> 21:36.560
Now look at social media.

21:37.200 --> 21:39.720
People aren't asking, is this how I feel?

21:40.020 --> 21:42.780
They're asking, how will this be received?

21:43.860 --> 21:45.180
They simplify themselves.

21:45.720 --> 21:47.100
They exaggerate themselves.

21:47.580 --> 21:49.660
They flatten their entire personality

21:49.660 --> 21:51.400
into something shareable,

21:51.780 --> 21:56.040
something the algorithm rewards, a like, a comment.

21:56.920 --> 21:59.300
Whatever gets rewarded, gets repeated.

22:00.000 --> 22:02.340
Whatever gets ignored, disappears.

22:03.360 --> 22:04.740
That's not self-expression.

22:05.200 --> 22:06.220
That's conditioning.

22:06.820 --> 22:09.400
Slow, methodical, and over time.

22:11.660 --> 22:13.800
Guy Debord wrote about this in 1967.

22:14.460 --> 22:17.100
He described the three stages of human degradation.

22:17.780 --> 22:19.160
First, being.

22:20.120 --> 22:21.820
You are what you are.

22:22.140 --> 22:23.140
Then, having.

22:23.800 --> 22:25.180
You are what you own.

22:25.700 --> 22:26.860
Finally, appearing.

22:27.720 --> 22:29.860
You are what you seem to be.

22:30.620 --> 22:34.240
He wrote, all that once was directly lived

22:34.240 --> 22:36.600
has become mere representation.

22:37.380 --> 22:40.780
He wrote that in 1967, before the internet,

22:41.320 --> 22:44.160
before social media, and before any of the algorithms.

22:44.780 --> 22:45.740
He saw it coming.

22:46.840 --> 22:49.760
And over time, when your external performance

22:49.760 --> 22:52.240
doesn't match your internal experience,

22:52.240 --> 22:54.800
there is one universal response.

22:56.800 --> 22:57.920
You feel hollow.

22:59.000 --> 23:01.520
Carl Jung called this losing yourself in the persona.

23:01.980 --> 23:02.700
The mask.

23:03.400 --> 23:05.080
The word literally comes from the mask

23:05.080 --> 23:06.680
actors wore in Greek theater.

23:07.460 --> 23:09.720
Jung said the danger isn't wearing the mask.

23:10.160 --> 23:13.360
The danger is forgetting it's a mask in the first place.

23:14.120 --> 23:15.940
And social media isn't just a mask.

23:16.680 --> 23:19.020
It's a mask that becomes your face.

23:20.280 --> 23:21.660
The cattle call.

23:22.560 --> 23:24.780
Once you're fed, fenced, and branded,

23:25.680 --> 23:29.880
you need to be kept moving in one direction together.

23:30.660 --> 23:32.960
And there's only one tool that moves a herd.

23:33.760 --> 23:34.180
Fear.

23:35.000 --> 23:37.080
And this isn't opinion, it's neuroscience.

23:38.040 --> 23:40.900
Your amygdala, the fear center of your brain,

23:41.500 --> 23:43.620
processes threats in milliseconds

23:43.620 --> 23:46.600
before your rational mind even activates.

23:47.440 --> 23:50.460
Daniel Goleman calls this the amygdala hijack.

23:50.860 --> 23:52.940
Your body enters fight or flight

23:52.940 --> 23:56.760
before you're even consciously aware of what scares you.

23:57.320 --> 23:59.140
And here's what makes this devastating.

24:00.240 --> 24:01.360
Your body can't tell the difference

24:01.360 --> 24:03.640
between a charging line and a news notification.

24:04.580 --> 24:06.400
The stress response is identical.

24:07.440 --> 24:10.120
Adrenaline, cortisol, heart rate spike,

24:10.840 --> 24:13.320
narrowed attention, rational thought suppressed.

24:14.380 --> 24:16.040
And when the stress becomes chronic,

24:16.040 --> 24:19.600
when you're living inside a 24-hour cycle of outrage,

24:20.120 --> 24:22.400
crisis, emergency, scandal,

24:23.320 --> 24:25.640
your brain physically changes shape.

24:26.000 --> 24:27.120
This is documented.

24:28.000 --> 24:29.920
The prefrontal cortex, the part of your brain

24:29.920 --> 24:31.600
responsible for rational thought,

24:31.960 --> 24:36.460
long-term planning, and nuanced thinking actually shrinks.

24:36.620 --> 24:38.620
The neural connections atrophy.

24:39.040 --> 24:42.660
Meanwhile, the amygdala, the fear center, it grows.

24:43.320 --> 24:44.740
The connections strengthen.

24:45.080 --> 24:48.980
You become structurally less capable of rational thought

24:48.980 --> 24:52.020
and structurally more reactive to fear.

24:53.720 --> 24:55.500
And this is not a character flaw.

24:56.200 --> 24:58.180
This is biology being exploited.

24:58.980 --> 25:00.920
And the platforms know it.

25:01.440 --> 25:04.020
Facebook's own data showed that fear-based content

25:04.020 --> 25:06.800
generates more engagement than any other emotion.

25:07.260 --> 25:09.860
It speeds reaction, it reduces nuance,

25:10.360 --> 25:13.820
it increases sharing, and it locks your memory in place.

25:14.320 --> 25:17.180
The system tracks what spikes your heart rate,

25:17.620 --> 25:19.740
what makes you comment, what makes you argue,

25:19.960 --> 25:23.720
what makes you angry, and it feeds you more and more of that.

25:24.440 --> 25:26.040
Every post is a potential trigger.

25:26.540 --> 25:28.420
Hate, panic, fear, anger.

25:28.780 --> 25:30.860
They all become advertising products.

25:31.840 --> 25:33.740
The longer you stay emotionally activated,

25:34.040 --> 25:37.100
the more valuable you become in real dollars.

25:37.700 --> 25:39.260
Cialdini calls it scarcity.

25:40.020 --> 25:43.220
When safety feels scarce, when time feels short,

25:43.220 --> 25:45.160
when the crisis feels urgent,

25:46.000 --> 25:48.040
people stop thinking and start reacting.

25:48.680 --> 25:50.860
They accept things they'd normally reject.

25:51.580 --> 25:53.880
They grant powers they'd normally question,

25:54.160 --> 25:55.500
and then they just comply.

25:56.220 --> 25:58.940
And this is why there's a new crisis every week,

25:59.200 --> 26:02.460
a new shortage, a new villain, a new emergency.

26:03.260 --> 26:05.940
Each one emotionally charging you

26:05.940 --> 26:07.660
to keep you at that heightened state.

26:08.200 --> 26:10.520
And it's immediately buried by the next one.

26:10.520 --> 26:13.480
You never get resolution, because resolution,

26:13.480 --> 26:16.040
it actually ends that engagement cycle,

26:16.460 --> 26:19.100
and it lowers that heightened emotion.

26:20.120 --> 26:21.220
And they can't have that.

26:21.320 --> 26:24.200
That's against their business model and their incentives.

26:27.180 --> 26:28.340
The auction.

26:31.780 --> 26:33.160
You are the product.

26:33.960 --> 26:37.080
Now, let me tell you what you're actually worth,

26:37.460 --> 26:39.680
not as a human being, as a product.

26:40.220 --> 26:42.240
Because that's what you are in the system.

26:42.980 --> 26:44.280
The platform isn't the product.

26:45.020 --> 26:46.560
The content isn't the product.

26:47.320 --> 26:50.540
You are the product, your attention, your engagement,

26:51.000 --> 26:53.100
your clicks, your comments, your shares.

26:54.560 --> 26:58.040
Shoshana Zuboff at Harvard named this surveillance capitalism.

26:58.960 --> 27:00.060
Here's how it works.

27:00.460 --> 27:03.400
Step one, your experience is raw material.

27:03.980 --> 27:06.800
Every click, every scroll, every pause,

27:06.800 --> 27:10.880
every hover, search, message, every location ping,

27:11.480 --> 27:12.320
all harvested.

27:13.260 --> 27:17.840
Step two, the data is refined into prediction products.

27:18.600 --> 27:21.640
Not just what you did, what you will do.

27:22.240 --> 27:26.060
Step three, the predictions are sold to business customers,

27:27.000 --> 27:30.320
advertisers, political campaigns, insurance companies,

27:31.180 --> 27:32.320
anyone willing to pay.

27:33.030 --> 27:36.400
Step four, this is where it crossed a line.

27:36.980 --> 27:39.580
The system evolves from predicting your behavior

27:39.580 --> 27:43.280
to modifying it, nudging it,

27:43.540 --> 27:46.280
tuning, hurting, conditioning you.

27:46.900 --> 27:50.340
What data scientists internally call actuating.

27:51.320 --> 27:55.480
You generate nearly 1.7 megabytes of data per second.

27:56.020 --> 27:59.480
Your average daily screen time is almost seven hours.

27:59.480 --> 28:03.880
Your attention span on social media is 8.25 seconds,

28:04.200 --> 28:06.580
down from 12 just 10 years ago.

28:07.460 --> 28:11.120
Cambridge Analytica harvested 87 million Facebook profiles

28:11.120 --> 28:12.440
through a single quiz app.

28:13.100 --> 28:15.780
They discovered that with just 10 Facebook likes,

28:16.340 --> 28:17.900
they could evaluate your personality

28:17.900 --> 28:19.600
more accurate than your coworkers,

28:20.280 --> 28:22.820
with 70 likes better than your close friends.

28:23.640 --> 28:26.220
On a single day in August 2016,

28:26.220 --> 28:30.840
one political campaign posted 100,000 ad variations

28:30.840 --> 28:32.180
on a single platform.

28:33.100 --> 28:36.020
Each voter saw individually tailored messages

28:36.020 --> 28:39.460
to exploit their specific psychological profile.

28:40.260 --> 28:41.480
You are not the customer.

28:42.100 --> 28:44.000
You are the livestock at auction.

28:44.760 --> 28:46.500
And Cialdini's principle of authority

28:46.880 --> 28:50.080
is what makes you trust the auctioneer.

28:50.300 --> 28:53.820
In the 1960s, Stanley Milgram ran an experiment at Yale.

28:53.820 --> 28:58.180
Ordinary people, teachers, postal workers, salespeople.

28:58.860 --> 29:00.620
They were told by a man in a lab coat

29:00.620 --> 29:03.240
to administer electric shock to a stranger.

29:03.980 --> 29:05.640
The shocks went up to 450 volts.

29:06.440 --> 29:08.800
The stranger screamed and begged him to stop.

29:09.980 --> 29:14.140
65% administered the full 450 volts.

29:14.820 --> 29:16.440
Not because they were sadists,

29:16.880 --> 29:20.380
but because an authority figure told them to do so.

29:21.960 --> 29:23.620
Milgram went on to write,

29:24.280 --> 29:26.340
ordinary people simply doing their jobs

29:26.340 --> 29:28.920
and without any particular hostility on their part

29:28.920 --> 29:32.460
can become agents in a terrible and destructive process.

29:34.700 --> 29:36.600
The tobacco industry understood this.

29:37.060 --> 29:40.700
In 1969, Brown and Williamson produced an internal memo.

29:41.260 --> 29:43.300
And I want you to hear the exact words.

29:44.040 --> 29:45.400
Doubt is our product.

29:45.740 --> 29:48.160
Since it is the best means of competing

29:48.160 --> 29:50.180
with the body of fact that exists

29:50.180 --> 29:51.880
in the mind of the general public.

29:52.520 --> 29:54.520
They didn't argue that cigarettes were safe.

29:55.120 --> 29:58.340
They simply manufactured doubt about the science.

29:58.900 --> 30:00.940
They created fake scientific organizations

30:00.940 --> 30:02.500
with legitimate sounding names.

30:02.860 --> 30:04.280
They funded junk studies.

30:04.620 --> 30:06.300
They attacked real scientists.

30:07.580 --> 30:10.720
And the fossil fuel industry adopted the identical playbook.

30:11.100 --> 30:14.200
Same PR firms, same research institutions,

30:14.880 --> 30:16.760
many of the same individual researchers.

30:17.420 --> 30:20.240
Authority is manufactured and once manufactured,

30:21.240 --> 30:22.820
it replaces evidence.

30:26.700 --> 30:27.900
The herder.

30:29.320 --> 30:30.660
Everything I've described so far,

30:30.860 --> 30:34.380
the food, the fences, the brands, the fear, the auction,

30:35.100 --> 30:38.720
all of it needs just one thing to function, a story.

30:39.440 --> 30:41.780
Because humans don't process the world through data,

30:42.060 --> 30:43.860
we process it through narrative.

30:44.660 --> 30:45.760
The wiring is ancient.

30:46.160 --> 30:47.360
It predates language

30:48.000 --> 30:51.300
and it's terrifyingly easy to hijack.

30:52.140 --> 30:54.760
There was a man who figured this out before anyone else.

30:55.080 --> 30:56.640
His name was Edward Bernays.

30:57.060 --> 30:59.540
He was Sigmund Freud's nephew, twice over.

31:00.500 --> 31:02.020
His mother was Freud's sister.

31:02.260 --> 31:04.840
His father was the brother of Freud's wife.

31:05.280 --> 31:06.800
Psychology was in the family business.

31:07.420 --> 31:11.020
In 1917, the United States entered World War I

31:11.020 --> 31:13.460
and created the Committee of Public Information.

31:13.850 --> 31:16.840
They deployed 75,000 civilian volunteers,

31:17.340 --> 31:18.580
the four-minute men,

31:19.320 --> 31:21.640
to give patriotic speeches in movie theaters

31:21.640 --> 31:23.440
while the film reels changed.

31:24.040 --> 31:26.820
They spoke to 314 million people.

31:27.300 --> 31:29.920
They produced posters, films, newspapers,

31:30.400 --> 31:33.080
all with one message, support the war.

31:34.000 --> 31:34.640
It worked.

31:35.120 --> 31:37.840
A nation that wanted nothing to do with the European war

31:37.840 --> 31:39.880
was mobilized in months.

31:40.500 --> 31:41.920
Bernays was a member of the committee.

31:42.420 --> 31:43.660
And after that war,

31:44.160 --> 31:46.180
he had an insight that changed everything.

31:47.120 --> 31:50.040
If propaganda works in wartime, why not peacetime?

31:50.900 --> 31:52.400
There was just one problem.

31:52.840 --> 31:55.620
The word propaganda had become toxic,

31:56.300 --> 31:58.380
especially after the Nazis used it openly.

31:59.040 --> 32:02.080
So Bernays did something brilliantly terrifying.

32:02.760 --> 32:04.260
He rebranded propaganda.

32:04.660 --> 32:06.860
He called it public relations.

32:07.780 --> 32:08.980
The substance was identical.

32:09.440 --> 32:10.700
The tools were identical.

32:10.700 --> 32:12.560
Only the word changed.

32:13.220 --> 32:14.220
And then he proved it worked.

32:14.680 --> 32:17.360
The American Tobacco Company wanted women to smoke,

32:18.040 --> 32:20.000
a taboo thing in the 1920s.

32:20.160 --> 32:22.980
Bernays consulted a psychologist who told him cigarettes

32:22.980 --> 32:25.900
could be reframed as symbols of female empowerment.

32:26.620 --> 32:28.560
So on Easter Sunday, 1929,

32:29.020 --> 32:31.120
he hired 30 beautiful debutantes

32:31.120 --> 32:34.500
to march in the New York Easter Parade, smoking cigarettes.

32:35.400 --> 32:37.480
His secretary posed as a woman's right activist

32:37.480 --> 32:38.340
to recruit them.

32:38.880 --> 32:41.420
No connection to the tobacco company was permitted.

32:42.120 --> 32:44.720
The New York Times, front page the next day,

32:45.460 --> 32:46.980
a group of girls puff on cigarettes

32:46.980 --> 32:48.780
as a gesture of freedom.

32:49.760 --> 32:50.640
He didn't sell cigarettes.

32:51.140 --> 32:52.440
He sold an identity.

32:53.300 --> 32:57.380
And women's cigarettes purchases nearly tripled in six years.

32:58.160 --> 32:59.220
He did it again with bacon.

32:59.980 --> 33:02.720
Americans used to eat light breakfasts.

33:02.940 --> 33:05.440
Bernays had a doctor write to 5,000 physicians

33:05.440 --> 33:08.440
asking if a heavier breakfast would be healthier.

33:09.180 --> 33:10.560
4,500 said yes.

33:11.100 --> 33:11.580
The headlines?

33:12.500 --> 33:17.060
4,500 physicians urge Americans to eat heavy breakfasts.

33:17.260 --> 33:19.460
Bacon and eggs became the American breakfast.

33:20.040 --> 33:22.220
A century later, we still eat it.

33:22.760 --> 33:23.940
He didn't advertise bacon.

33:24.180 --> 33:26.640
He manufactured medical consensus.

33:27.540 --> 33:29.720
And then, and this is the one that shows you

33:29.720 --> 33:30.780
how far this goes,

33:31.620 --> 33:33.160
the United Fruit Company hired him

33:33.160 --> 33:35.020
because Guatemala's elected president

33:35.020 --> 33:37.000
was threatening their land holdings

33:37.000 --> 33:38.800
with agricultural reform.

33:39.620 --> 33:41.700
Bernays orchestrated a media campaign

33:41.700 --> 33:45.120
painting the Guatemalan government as communist threats.

33:46.860 --> 33:48.980
He flew journalists from the New York Times

33:48.980 --> 33:51.940
and Time Magazine to Central America on the company's dime.

33:52.380 --> 33:54.480
He fed them a narrative of communist terror.

33:55.040 --> 33:59.120
By 1954, the CIA overthrew Guatemala's

33:59.120 --> 34:00.500
democratically elected government.

34:01.320 --> 34:03.420
Bernays, he didn't fire a shot.

34:03.840 --> 34:04.680
He didn't need to.

34:04.880 --> 34:06.140
He just told a story

34:06.600 --> 34:09.760
and the story did all the legwork for him.

34:10.200 --> 34:12.220
And remember those heuristics I told you about?

34:12.400 --> 34:13.380
The mental shortcuts?

34:14.140 --> 34:15.600
This is where they become weapons.

34:16.360 --> 34:18.060
Bernays didn't argue for cigarettes.

34:18.460 --> 34:19.680
He just presented data.

34:20.560 --> 34:21.960
He didn't make a logical case.

34:22.240 --> 34:23.900
He triggered system one.

34:24.500 --> 34:26.620
He used the availability heuristics,

34:27.100 --> 34:29.040
put smoking women in the front stage

34:29.040 --> 34:31.660
of every newspaper and suddenly female smoking

34:31.660 --> 34:34.060
felt common, normal, inevitable.

34:34.920 --> 34:35.960
The more you see something,

34:36.160 --> 34:39.000
the more your brain codes it as reality.

34:39.860 --> 34:41.200
He used anchoring.

34:41.920 --> 34:43.900
The first frame you receive about an event

34:43.900 --> 34:46.220
determines everything you think about it afterward.

34:46.860 --> 34:48.500
He anchored cigarettes to freedom.

34:49.440 --> 34:52.900
Before anyone could actually anchor them to cancer.

34:53.560 --> 34:55.940
He anchored Guatemala to communism

34:55.940 --> 34:59.680
before anyone could anchor it to agricultural reform.

35:01.060 --> 35:02.000
He used framing.

35:02.800 --> 35:05.200
The same act, women smoking in public,

35:05.660 --> 35:08.300
frame as rebellion against patriarchy

35:08.300 --> 35:10.840
instead of corporate profit strategy.

35:11.180 --> 35:13.800
Produces completely different emotional responses.

35:14.380 --> 35:16.960
Same event, different frame, different reality.

35:17.840 --> 35:19.740
And here's the part that connects everything.

35:20.200 --> 35:22.200
Heuristics are faster than thought.

35:22.800 --> 35:24.980
Your brain processes a frame and anchor

35:24.980 --> 35:27.440
an available image in milliseconds

35:27.440 --> 35:29.960
before your conscious mind can actually intervene.

35:30.460 --> 35:33.860
By the time system two activates, if it activates at all,

35:34.160 --> 35:36.900
system one has already decided how you feel.

35:38.020 --> 35:40.320
That's why Bernays didn't need to convince anyone.

35:40.540 --> 35:42.280
He just needed to get there first.

35:44.020 --> 35:45.940
This is called Cialdini's principle of liking.

35:46.760 --> 35:48.160
You don't need to trust the message.

35:48.380 --> 35:50.200
You just need to like the messenger,

35:50.940 --> 35:53.180
a relatable anchor, a friendly face,

35:53.580 --> 35:56.080
or possibly even a parasocial relationship,

35:56.540 --> 35:58.060
a one-sided emotional bond

35:58.060 --> 35:59.700
where you feel like you know someone

35:59.700 --> 36:01.840
who doesn't even know you exist.

36:03.140 --> 36:05.020
Research shows that parasocial relationships

36:05.020 --> 36:08.520
viewers formed with one particular reality TV host

36:08.520 --> 36:11.100
directly contributed to its political popularity.

36:11.880 --> 36:13.700
The more intense the parasocial bond,

36:14.300 --> 36:15.720
the more forgiving viewers

36:15.720 --> 36:17.800
were of his controversial statements.

36:18.360 --> 36:19.920
You didn't evaluate his policies.

36:19.920 --> 36:24.420
You liked him and liking bypasses evaluation.

36:25.620 --> 36:27.660
Chomsky mapped this entire system in 1988.

36:28.220 --> 36:30.420
He called it manufacturing consent

36:30.420 --> 36:32.480
and identifying five filters

36:32.480 --> 36:34.740
that every piece of information passes through

36:34.740 --> 36:36.640
before it reaches you.

36:37.380 --> 36:40.020
Ownership, who profits from this story?

36:40.820 --> 36:44.460
Advertising, who keeps paying to keep this outlet alive?

36:45.080 --> 36:48.620
Sourcing, whose version of events is being reported?

36:49.680 --> 36:50.400
Flak.

36:51.180 --> 36:53.760
What happens to the outlets that challenge the narrative?

36:54.500 --> 36:54.840
Beer.

36:55.700 --> 36:58.540
What's the boogeyman that makes dissent sound unpatriotic?

37:00.120 --> 37:02.400
The system doesn't even require conspiracy.

37:02.860 --> 37:04.300
It works through market forces,

37:04.960 --> 37:07.620
internalized assumptions, and self-censorship.

37:08.220 --> 37:10.360
Journalists don't receive orders to suppress stories.

37:10.720 --> 37:13.240
They learn which stories advance careers

37:13.240 --> 37:14.600
and which ones don't.

37:14.600 --> 37:18.780
The result is propaganda without the propagandist,

37:19.260 --> 37:21.700
a machine that runs itself.

37:23.820 --> 37:25.100
The stampede.

37:27.280 --> 37:28.980
Now, the final mechanism.

37:29.660 --> 37:33.080
Once the herd is fed, fenced, branded, frightened,

37:33.620 --> 37:37.840
sold, and storied, there's only one thing left to do.

37:38.360 --> 37:39.520
Split it.

37:39.740 --> 37:41.680
Because a herd that fights itself

37:41.680 --> 37:43.460
never looks up at the rancher.

37:44.000 --> 37:47.560
This is what Cialdini's seventh principle is, unity.

37:48.540 --> 37:50.340
And it's the most dangerous one.

37:50.820 --> 37:52.720
Unity isn't about liking someone.

37:53.080 --> 37:55.660
It's about feeling they are one of us.

37:56.140 --> 37:58.220
It operates at the level of we.

37:59.020 --> 38:02.060
When unity is activated, people will do things for us

38:02.060 --> 38:03.920
that they would never do for a stranger.

38:04.780 --> 38:06.140
They will lie for the group.

38:06.980 --> 38:09.240
Psychologists call this blue lies,

38:09.920 --> 38:13.060
deliberate falsehoods to protect the in-group.

38:13.620 --> 38:15.460
When group loyalty trumps truth,

38:15.860 --> 38:18.300
lying for the tribe feels normal.

38:19.140 --> 38:22.800
It even feels morally superior to telling the truth.

38:25.240 --> 38:26.820
Henry Toschfeld actually proved

38:26.820 --> 38:28.720
you can create in-group hostility

38:28.720 --> 38:31.360
with completely arbitrary distinctions.

38:32.020 --> 38:34.440
He randomly assigned people to meaningless groups

38:34.700 --> 38:37.120
and they immediately developed bias.

38:37.780 --> 38:42.800
No history, no grievance, no ideology, just us versus them.

38:43.600 --> 38:45.680
Now take that instinct and feed it through

38:45.680 --> 38:48.100
an algorithm designed to maximize engagement

38:48.100 --> 38:50.420
through emotional provocation.

38:50.840 --> 38:55.260
Left versus right, red versus blue, us versus them.

38:56.060 --> 38:59.740
This isn't politics, this is audience segmentation.

39:00.200 --> 39:03.440
Two simplified tribes, two emotional markets,

39:03.440 --> 39:06.900
two predictable reaction sets.

39:07.560 --> 39:10.100
And while the two halves of the herd fight each other,

39:10.440 --> 39:12.800
nothing upstream is ever examined.

39:13.680 --> 39:15.280
The Russian Internet Research Agency

39:15.280 --> 39:16.680
understood this perfectly.

39:17.120 --> 39:20.300
Starting in 2013, they created fake communities

39:20.300 --> 39:22.300
across the entire political spectrum.

39:23.140 --> 39:25.700
United Muslims of America, 300,000 followers.

39:26.360 --> 39:28.800
Secured Borders, 130,000 followers.

39:28.800 --> 39:33.540
They reached up to 126 million Americans on Facebook alone.

39:34.300 --> 39:36.440
The goal was never to support one side.

39:36.940 --> 39:40.780
The goal was to make both sides hate each other even more

39:40.780 --> 39:43.560
because division is the product.

39:44.720 --> 39:47.540
And once the herd is divided, the ranchers can perform.

39:48.400 --> 39:51.460
Modern politics is not a system for solving problems.

39:51.880 --> 39:54.960
It's a stage with roles and costumes

39:54.960 --> 39:57.060
and predictable conflict arcs.

39:57.060 --> 39:59.440
This is why congressional hearings look dramatic

39:59.440 --> 40:01.040
and accomplish almost nothing.

40:02.440 --> 40:04.000
Take Mark Zuckerberg, for example.

40:04.580 --> 40:07.120
He testified before Congress multiple times.

40:07.520 --> 40:09.280
Each time, angry questions.

40:09.800 --> 40:11.520
Each time, solemn promises.

40:12.060 --> 40:16.080
After years of hearings, Congress still has yet to pass

40:16.080 --> 40:17.700
a single comprehensive law

40:17.700 --> 40:19.700
governing online platforms today.

40:21.020 --> 40:22.340
One parent at a hearing said,

40:23.060 --> 40:24.360
nothing that was said today

40:24.360 --> 40:25.920
was different than what we expected.

40:26.250 --> 40:28.580
A lot of promises and a lot of talk

40:28.580 --> 40:31.580
without them really saying anything.

40:33.020 --> 40:34.920
Wells Fargo, they created millions

40:34.920 --> 40:36.200
of fraudulent bank accounts.

40:36.700 --> 40:37.740
The hearing went viral.

40:38.300 --> 40:39.340
The CEO was grilled.

40:39.820 --> 40:42.560
And then, nothing structural changed.

40:43.920 --> 40:46.280
The Roman Senate operated the same way.

40:46.660 --> 40:49.900
Stripped of real power, it continued to perform governance.

40:50.600 --> 40:53.020
Augustus controlled membership of the Senate itself.

40:53.820 --> 40:57.020
Every senator's career depended on his goodwill.

40:57.720 --> 41:01.860
But the Senate still convened, still debated, still voted.

41:02.420 --> 41:04.620
Because the appearance of shared government

41:04.620 --> 41:06.900
was more valuable to the emperor

41:06.900 --> 41:08.680
than dissolving it altogether.

41:09.660 --> 41:12.140
The Senate told citizens the republic still existed,

41:12.400 --> 41:13.380
but it didn't.

41:13.700 --> 41:15.820
And congressional hearings tell citizens

41:15.820 --> 41:17.680
that accountability still exists.

41:18.140 --> 41:19.220
But does it?

41:20.060 --> 41:21.840
If politics were about results,

41:22.340 --> 41:24.740
it wouldn't need an audience.

41:27.000 --> 41:27.940
The scar.

41:31.820 --> 41:33.300
I need to tell you something now.

41:33.500 --> 41:34.300
Something personal.

41:35.080 --> 41:36.600
Everything I just described to you,

41:36.840 --> 41:39.380
the feet, the trough, the fence,

41:40.480 --> 41:42.140
the branding iron, the cattle call,

41:42.340 --> 41:45.180
the auction, the herder, the stampede.

41:45.760 --> 41:47.400
I didn't learn that from a textbook.

41:48.000 --> 41:49.800
I learned it from my own bloodline.

41:50.480 --> 41:52.660
My people were the first heard.

41:53.400 --> 41:56.640
The colonization of indigenous people in North America

41:56.640 --> 41:59.240
followed every single step I just outlined

41:59.240 --> 42:04.280
in the exact same order, with the same exact logic.

42:04.820 --> 42:06.580
And I need you to understand,

42:06.980 --> 42:10.380
this was an ancient history done by people in funny hats.

42:11.220 --> 42:16.120
This was systematic, documented, deliberate, and it worked.

42:17.940 --> 42:18.860
Step one.

42:19.240 --> 42:20.760
They told a story.

42:22.380 --> 42:24.280
Before a single shot was fired,

42:24.840 --> 42:26.620
before a single child was taken,

42:27.060 --> 42:28.220
they needed permission.

42:29.120 --> 42:30.280
The pope wrote it.

42:30.680 --> 42:35.120
In 1452, 1455, and 1493,

42:36.180 --> 42:37.960
a series of papal declarations,

42:38.100 --> 42:39.240
the doctrine of discovery,

42:39.820 --> 42:42.980
stated that any land not occupied by Christians

42:42.980 --> 42:45.720
was terra nullius.

42:46.500 --> 42:47.960
Empty, available,

42:48.940 --> 42:51.700
even if millions of people already lived there.

42:52.280 --> 42:55.240
A story written by a pope gave an entire continent

42:55.240 --> 42:57.520
permission to steal a hemisphere.

42:58.360 --> 43:01.320
The Vatican didn't formally repudiate this until 2023.

43:02.980 --> 43:03.700
2023.

43:05.220 --> 43:06.200
Let that sink in.

43:07.960 --> 43:08.740
Step two.

43:09.180 --> 43:10.460
They changed the language.

43:11.440 --> 43:13.880
Indigenous people were rewritten as savages.

43:14.190 --> 43:16.360
The Declaration of Independence itself,

43:16.560 --> 43:18.480
the document you were taught to revere,

43:18.900 --> 43:21.800
refers to merciless Indian savages.

43:22.440 --> 43:23.360
That's not a footnote.

43:24.120 --> 43:25.760
That's the founding document.

43:26.440 --> 43:28.020
The language of dehumanization

43:28.020 --> 43:30.940
is built into the origin story of this country.

43:32.460 --> 43:33.800
Step three.

43:34.040 --> 43:36.620
They named the violence something beautiful.

43:37.940 --> 43:39.020
Manifest Destiny.

43:39.860 --> 43:41.920
Yeah, that was coined in 1845.

43:42.640 --> 43:46.260
Continental theft rebranded as divine mission.

43:46.640 --> 43:47.360
God's will.

43:47.880 --> 43:48.500
Progress.

43:49.180 --> 43:50.100
Civilization.

43:50.860 --> 43:52.900
The paintings from that era show it.

43:53.220 --> 43:56.140
A glowing white figure leading settlers westward

43:56.140 --> 43:58.880
while native peoples are pushed into darkness.

43:59.880 --> 44:02.420
Genocide was rebranded as progress.

44:03.940 --> 44:04.600
Step four.

44:05.180 --> 44:08.320
They made promises they never even intended to keep.

44:09.020 --> 44:12.040
Between 1778 and 1871,

44:12.620 --> 44:15.460
the United States signed 368 treaties

44:15.460 --> 44:16.800
with indigenous nations.

44:17.480 --> 44:20.900
Because we were independent nations, sovereign peoples,

44:21.540 --> 44:22.880
every single treaty was broken.

44:23.620 --> 44:25.660
Every single one.

44:27.100 --> 44:29.080
The Fort Laramie Treaty of 1868

44:29.080 --> 44:33.780
guaranteed the Sioux the Black Hills in perpetuity.

44:34.460 --> 44:37.540
When gold was discovered, they redrew the boundaries,

44:37.940 --> 44:42.320
more than 1.5 billion acres were taken through treaties

44:42.320 --> 44:45.440
the U.S. had no intention of honoring in the first place.

44:45.860 --> 44:49.100
Treaties weren't agreements, they were tools of delay.

44:49.840 --> 44:53.120
By time, until the military can actually finish the job,

44:53.780 --> 44:55.680
the promises, they were the weapon,

44:56.380 --> 44:57.880
and everybody was fooled.

44:59.500 --> 45:00.360
Step five.

45:01.140 --> 45:02.640
They destroyed the food supply.

45:03.500 --> 45:06.020
Colonel Richard Dodge, 1867.

45:06.900 --> 45:09.700
Every buffalo dead is an Indian gone.

45:10.560 --> 45:14.800
General Philip Sarden told the Texas legislature in 1875,

45:15.440 --> 45:18.080
these men have done more in the last two years

45:18.080 --> 45:20.100
to settle the vexed Indian question

45:20.100 --> 45:24.340
than the entire regular army has done in the last 40 years.

45:25.140 --> 45:27.260
They are destroying the Indians commissary.

45:28.960 --> 45:32.020
The U.S. Army provided the ammunition to buffalo hunters.

45:32.620 --> 45:34.300
The destruction was systematic.

45:34.790 --> 45:37.220
South herds, then the North herds.

45:38.400 --> 45:41.040
An entire species driven to the edge of extinction.

45:41.960 --> 45:43.140
This wasn't commercial hunting,

45:43.600 --> 45:47.040
this was economic warfare disguised as commerce.

45:47.740 --> 45:50.140
Genocide through starvation.

45:50.740 --> 45:51.540
Step six.

45:52.220 --> 45:54.060
They contained and monitored.

45:55.300 --> 45:56.080
Reservations.

45:56.740 --> 45:59.680
The worst land, stripped of all of its resources,

46:00.220 --> 46:03.140
dependent on government rations, behavior supervised,

46:03.680 --> 46:07.100
movement restricted, a cage that was built,

46:07.760 --> 46:09.580
and they called it a home.

46:11.020 --> 46:11.860
Step seven.

46:12.520 --> 46:13.700
They took the children.

46:15.180 --> 46:17.280
Killed the Indian, saved the man.

46:18.020 --> 46:23.480
400 schools, 150 years, tens of thousands of children,

46:24.160 --> 46:27.700
names erased, languages beaten out of them, haircut,

46:28.380 --> 46:30.780
a spiritual violation treated as hygiene,

46:31.420 --> 46:34.080
spiritual practices criminalized and replaced.

46:34.840 --> 46:39.380
At Carlisle alone, at least 186 children died.

46:40.160 --> 46:41.720
Buried in the school cemetery,

46:42.280 --> 46:43.780
never returned to their families.

46:44.600 --> 46:46.000
One survivor testifies,

46:46.800 --> 46:48.740
if we were not finished scrubbing floors

46:48.740 --> 46:49.900
when the whistle sounded,

46:50.900 --> 46:53.260
the matron would go around strapping us

46:53.260 --> 46:55.720
while we were still on our hands and knees.

46:56.620 --> 46:57.920
And the trauma?

46:58.440 --> 47:00.320
That didn't end when schools closed.

47:01.080 --> 47:04.940
Epigenetic research, the study of how trauma modifies DNA,

47:05.640 --> 47:08.880
shows the severe stress leaves a biological echo

47:08.880 --> 47:10.260
in future generations.

47:11.060 --> 47:13.000
The children of boarding school survivors

47:13.000 --> 47:16.680
carry that trauma in their sails to this day.

47:17.260 --> 47:19.640
Families where multiple generations attended these schools

47:19.640 --> 47:22.260
report greater psychological distress

47:22.260 --> 47:25.180
than families where only one generation did.

47:26.100 --> 47:28.280
The system was so effective

47:28.280 --> 47:30.540
that it actually changed our biology

47:30.540 --> 47:32.920
in the most horrific way possible.

47:34.140 --> 47:35.420
So when someone tells me

47:35.420 --> 47:37.880
that I'm describing the manipulation, the control,

47:38.340 --> 47:40.580
the narrative warfare, the identity destruction,

47:41.040 --> 47:44.520
as paranoia or a conspiracy theory or an exaggeration,

47:44.940 --> 47:46.740
you know what, I don't even argue with them.

47:47.000 --> 47:49.120
I just know they haven't seen the scar

47:49.120 --> 47:51.700
because I was born with it.

47:51.780 --> 47:54.240
I was born into it.

47:55.100 --> 47:56.260
The unbrand.

47:58.600 --> 48:00.000
I wanna come back to where we started.

48:01.020 --> 48:03.160
A harmless man is not a good man.

48:03.680 --> 48:06.360
A good man is a very, very dangerous man

48:06.360 --> 48:08.860
who has that under voluntary control.

48:09.800 --> 48:11.600
Carl Jung, the psychologist,

48:12.160 --> 48:14.020
whose work Peterson is drawing from,

48:14.520 --> 48:17.060
said something I think about all the time.

48:17.680 --> 48:20.620
You should be a monster, an absolute monster,

48:20.920 --> 48:23.460
and then you should learn to control it.

48:23.840 --> 48:25.360
He wasn't talking about violence.

48:25.740 --> 48:27.540
He was talking about capacity,

48:28.420 --> 48:30.820
the integration of what he called the shadow,

48:31.260 --> 48:34.280
the parts of yourself you've been conditioned to suppress,

48:34.860 --> 48:36.800
deny, flatten, and hide.

48:37.800 --> 48:41.180
He said, you cannot have proper respect for yourself

48:41.180 --> 48:42.900
until you know that you're a monster

48:43.700 --> 48:45.800
because you won't act carefully enough.

48:46.560 --> 48:48.660
And that's what the system does.

48:49.140 --> 48:50.920
At least that's what it intends to do.

48:51.320 --> 48:52.680
It doesn't make you evil.

48:52.680 --> 48:54.460
It makes you harmless.

48:55.380 --> 48:56.540
It simplifies you.

48:56.680 --> 48:58.100
It flattens you,

48:58.500 --> 48:59.740
sorts you into a category,

48:59.940 --> 49:01.580
gives you a label that fits in a bin,

49:02.200 --> 49:03.740
feeds you content that confirms

49:03.740 --> 49:05.220
what you've already believed,

49:06.140 --> 49:07.380
frightens you into compliance,

49:08.200 --> 49:10.060
sells your attention to the highest bidder,

49:10.360 --> 49:13.140
and tells you a story about yourself that feels true

49:13.140 --> 49:15.500
but was written by someone else.

49:16.600 --> 49:18.480
You weren't born to be content,

49:19.140 --> 49:20.800
not the emotion, the product.

49:21.900 --> 49:24.980
Jean Baudrillard, the philosopher whose book

49:24.980 --> 49:28.600
Semilacra Simulation, literally inspired The Matrix.

49:29.180 --> 49:31.320
He said something that the Wachowskis

49:31.320 --> 49:32.640
didn't put into the movie.

49:33.200 --> 49:34.720
When they finished the first film,

49:35.060 --> 49:37.720
they invited him to consult on the sequels.

49:37.820 --> 49:39.120
He turned them down.

49:39.500 --> 49:41.780
He said, The Matrix got it wrong

49:42.240 --> 49:44.820
because the movie shows you a real world

49:44.820 --> 49:48.360
outside the simulation, a place you can escape to.

49:48.360 --> 49:51.420
Baudrillard said, there is no outside.

49:52.220 --> 49:54.680
The simulation and reality have merged.

49:55.300 --> 49:57.160
There's no red pill because the distinction

49:57.160 --> 50:00.300
between The Matrix and the real has collapsed.

50:01.720 --> 50:04.220
But I actually tend to disagree with them,

50:04.400 --> 50:06.860
not philosophically, experientially,

50:07.480 --> 50:10.280
because my people survived the original simulation.

50:11.020 --> 50:13.040
The colonization playbook was designed

50:13.040 --> 50:15.460
to replace our whole entire reality.

50:15.880 --> 50:18.160
Our names, our language, our spirituality,

50:18.860 --> 50:22.140
our relationship to the land with someone else's version.

50:22.140 --> 50:26.420
And it almost worked, but it didn't.

50:26.780 --> 50:29.720
Not for everybody, because some of my people

50:29.720 --> 50:31.600
refused the replacement.

50:32.480 --> 50:35.520
Zit Kalasha, the girl named Gertrude.

50:35.960 --> 50:37.740
She grew her hair long again.

50:38.260 --> 50:40.620
She spent her life fighting for the native rights.

50:41.560 --> 50:43.840
A single act, like growing your hair back,

50:44.340 --> 50:47.340
that wasn't just an act, it's a refusal.

50:47.760 --> 50:51.600
It says, your version of me is not me.

50:52.180 --> 50:55.940
Our language has survived, not in textbooks, in whispers.

50:56.680 --> 50:58.420
Grandmothers who spoke them in kitchens

50:58.420 --> 51:00.240
when no official was listening.

51:01.140 --> 51:03.380
Ceremonies that went underground for decades

51:03.380 --> 51:04.540
and then resurfaced.

51:05.200 --> 51:11.600
There's a Lakota phrase, mitokoya oyasin, all my relations.

51:12.270 --> 51:14.120
It means everything is connected,

51:14.780 --> 51:17.220
not metaphorically, structurally.

51:17.900 --> 51:20.620
When one is in pain, all are harmed.

51:21.320 --> 51:22.860
When there is justice for one,

51:23.680 --> 51:25.540
there is more justice for all.

51:26.340 --> 51:28.580
The phrase is the opposite of the algorithm.

51:29.460 --> 51:33.500
The algorithm atomizes you, isolates you,

51:33.860 --> 51:35.160
makes you a data point.

51:35.620 --> 51:39.940
Mitokoya oyasin makes isolation impossible.

51:40.660 --> 51:43.800
The colonization playbook requires atomized individuals.

51:44.660 --> 51:46.840
Isolated people are controllable people.

51:47.400 --> 51:49.920
Connected people are dangerous.

51:51.220 --> 51:53.480
Plato wrote about this 2,400 years ago.

51:54.140 --> 51:55.880
Prisoners chained inside a cave,

51:56.160 --> 51:57.440
watching shadows on a wall,

51:57.860 --> 51:59.840
believing the shadows were reality.

52:00.460 --> 52:03.380
One prisoner is freed, dragged into the sunlight,

52:03.760 --> 52:06.120
the light blinds, it actually hurts.

52:06.660 --> 52:07.960
And when the prisoner freed,

52:07.960 --> 52:09.860
returns for the other prisoners

52:09.860 --> 52:12.780
to tell the others what's actually real,

52:13.160 --> 52:14.600
they didn't believe them.

52:15.280 --> 52:17.500
In some versions of the story, they kill them.

52:18.040 --> 52:19.460
I'm not asking you to fight the cave.

52:20.160 --> 52:21.900
I'm not asking you to rage against the shadows.

52:22.800 --> 52:25.480
I'm not even asking you to do anything.

52:26.440 --> 52:27.980
Remember what I told you about in the beginning,

52:28.380 --> 52:29.100
about your eyes?

52:29.640 --> 52:32.460
Your brain processes images in 13 milliseconds,

52:32.880 --> 52:34.640
30 times faster than you can blink.

52:35.120 --> 52:37.060
Half your brain is dedicated to sight.

52:37.620 --> 52:40.280
80% of your reasoning flows through vision.

52:40.720 --> 52:46.320
And your eyes, yeah, they only see 0.0035% of what exists.

52:47.220 --> 52:49.800
You built your entire world on this sliver.

52:50.560 --> 52:53.300
And then a system that was built on top of that sliver,

52:53.780 --> 52:57.780
a system of symbols, narratives, algorithms, and frames

52:58.500 --> 53:00.320
that narrows it even further.

53:01.020 --> 53:03.080
That takes the tiny fraction of reality

53:03.080 --> 53:05.640
that you can perceive and curate it.

53:05.640 --> 53:08.260
It filters it, it sorts it,

53:08.500 --> 53:11.500
and decides what you see and what you don't.

53:11.660 --> 53:15.240
You're not seeing 0.0035% of reality anymore.

53:16.120 --> 53:19.300
You're seeing 0.0035% of reality

53:19.300 --> 53:22.080
filtered through someone else's interests.

53:23.720 --> 53:25.420
But here's what Plato understood,

53:26.020 --> 53:28.180
and what my people have always known.

53:28.820 --> 53:31.920
The limitation of your eyes is not the end of the story.

53:32.240 --> 53:33.260
It's just the beginning.

53:33.880 --> 53:35.440
Because there are ways of seeing

53:35.440 --> 53:37.200
that don't come through the eyes.

53:37.640 --> 53:40.000
Oral tradition, direct experience,

53:40.720 --> 53:43.440
relationship with your land, ceremony,

53:44.300 --> 53:48.140
silence, the kind of knowing that doesn't need a screen.

53:48.820 --> 53:49.740
It doesn't need a feed.

53:50.040 --> 53:52.280
It doesn't need an algorithm to validate it.

53:52.920 --> 53:55.540
My ancestors built entire civilizations

53:55.540 --> 53:59.980
on ways of knowing that bypass the visual sliver entirely.

53:59.980 --> 54:02.500
They didn't need to see the full spectrum.

54:03.360 --> 54:05.580
They needed to listen, to feel,

54:06.440 --> 54:07.440
to be in a relationship

54:07.440 --> 54:09.500
with something larger than themselves.

54:10.580 --> 54:15.160
Mitakuye Oyasin, all my relations isn't visual.

54:16.140 --> 54:19.400
It's a way of perceiving that the electromagnetic spectrum

54:19.980 --> 54:23.440
can't measure and the algorithm can't contain.

54:24.200 --> 54:26.460
So when I say I'm asking you to see,

54:26.920 --> 54:28.200
I don't mean see with your eyes.

54:28.900 --> 54:31.780
I mean with everything your eyes were designed to miss.

54:32.380 --> 54:33.940
I'm asking you to see.

54:34.740 --> 54:36.060
See the feed for what it is.

54:36.360 --> 54:37.040
See the fence.

54:37.680 --> 54:39.040
Feel the brand on your skin.

54:39.740 --> 54:40.700
Hear the cattle call.

54:41.640 --> 54:43.820
Understand what you're worth at the auction.

54:44.760 --> 54:46.200
Recognize the herder's voice.

54:47.120 --> 54:48.540
And when they try to stampede you

54:48.540 --> 54:51.500
into the other half of the herd, stand still.

54:53.580 --> 54:55.280
Because once you see the machinery,

54:55.820 --> 54:57.820
the performance stops working the same way.

54:57.820 --> 55:00.260
The outrage feels manufactured.

55:00.780 --> 55:02.320
The urgency feels engineered.

55:02.860 --> 55:04.660
The vision feels designed.

55:05.500 --> 55:08.380
And something underneath all of it becomes visible again.

55:08.820 --> 55:11.760
Something that was always there that you just didn't see.

55:12.540 --> 55:16.060
Under the noise, under the symbols, under that brand.

55:16.980 --> 55:17.340
You.

55:18.120 --> 55:19.980
Not the algorithms version of you.

55:20.200 --> 55:23.620
Not the profile, not the bio, not the label.

55:24.280 --> 55:24.780
You.

55:25.600 --> 55:27.220
My people have a word for what happens

55:27.220 --> 55:29.240
when the brand finally heals.

55:29.980 --> 55:31.940
It's called McWindon.

55:33.060 --> 55:34.020
Remembering.

